[199.468635, "o", "{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_012gvDjJZafAjJrBRjghM1ga\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Scenario Builder — Summary\\n2\\t\\n3\\t## Bug Fix\\n4\\t\\n5\\t### Priority 1 — IDA* heuristic reads wrong radio group\\n6\\t- **File:** `visual/js/panel.js:160`\\n7\\t- **Fix:** Changed `$('input[name=jump_point_heuristic]:checked')` → `$('input[name=ida_heuristic]:checked')`\\n8\\t- **Impact:** IDA* panel was reading JPS heuristic radio group instead of its own. User-selected heuristic in IDA* section was ignored.\\n9\\t\\n10\\t## Test Scenarios Created\\n11\\t\\n12\\t**File:** `test/VisualScenarios.js` — 39 tests across 14 priority scenarios.\\n13\\t\\n14\\t| Priority | Scenario | Tests | Status |\\n15\\t|----------|----------|-------|--------|\\n16\\t| 1 | IDA* heuristic independence | 2 | ✅ Pass |\\n17\\t| 2 | No path found (start surrounded) | 4 | ✅ Pass |\\n18\\t| 3 | Start equals end | 5 | ✅ Pass |\\n19\\t| 4 | Drag during search (state machine) | 1 | ✅ Documented |\\n20\\t| 5 | Wall on s"]
[199.469016, "o", "tart/end position | 4 | ✅ Pass |\\n21\\t| 6 | Pause/Resume cycle | 1 | ✅ Documented |\\n22\\t| 7 | Restart during search | 1 | ✅ Documented |\\n23\\t| 8 | JPS all 4 diagonal modes | 4 | ✅ Pass |\\n24\\t| 9 | Bi-directional vs unidirectional | 1 | ✅ Pass |\\n25\\t| 10 | Weight parameter effect | 1 | ✅ Pass |\\n26\\t| 11 | IDA* time limit | 3 | ✅ Pass |\\n27\\t| 12 | Full grid walls | 3 | ✅ Pass |\\n28\\t| 13 | Large grid performance (64×36) | 2 | ✅ Pass |\\n29\\t| 14 | Adjacent start/end | 4 | ✅ Pass |\\n30\\t\\n31\\t## Key Findings\\n32\\t\\n33\\t1. **Finders don't validate start/end walkability.** They push start into open list unconditionally. Visual app handles this via `isStartOrEndPos` guard in `mousedown` handler.\\n34\\t\\n35\\t2. **JPS UI gap confirmed.** Only `IfAtMostOneObstacle` and `Never` exposed. `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` work at library level but need UI dropdown to be selectable. Panel.js hardcodes `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` at line 139.\\n36\\t\\n37\\t3. **State machine correctly guar"]
[199.469656, "o", "ds drag.** `dragStart`/`dragEnd` only allowed from `ready`/`finished` states. No drag possible during `searching`/`paused`.\\n38\\t\\n39\\t4. **Pause/resume is clean.** `loop()` checks `Controller.is('searching')` — pausing stops the loop, resume re-enters it from same operations array position.\\n40\\t\\n41\\t5. **No \\\"path not found\\\" UI feedback.** `view.js:drawPath` returns silently on empty path. `showStats` shows `length: 0` but no explicit message. This is a UI gap, not a library bug.\\n42\\t\\n43\\t## Full Suite Result\\n44\\t\\n45\\t```\\n46\\t256 passing (1s)\\n47\\t0 failing\\n48\\t```\\n49\\t\\n50\\tNo regressions introduced.\\n51\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"562dad89-9e59-45fb-92c2-a22bcc008388\",\"uuid\":\"e129d868-bf9a-4b28-bb80-ceec6d595d2c\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-16T14:39:10.532Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/scenario-builder/output/summary.md\",\"content\":\"# Scenario Builder — Summary\\n"]
[199.469916, "o", "\\n## Bug Fix\\n\\n### Priority 1 — IDA* heuristic reads wrong radio group\\n- **File:** `visual/js/panel.js:160`\\n- **Fix:** Changed `$('input[name=jump_point_heuristic]:checked')` → `$('input[name=ida_heuristic]:checked')`\\n- **Impact:** IDA* panel was reading JPS heuristic radio group instead of its own. User-selected heuristic in IDA* section was ignored.\\n\\n## Test Scenarios Created\\n\\n**File:** `test/VisualScenarios.js` — 39 tests across 14 priority scenarios.\\n\\n| Priority | Scenario | Tests | Status |\\n|----------|----------|-------|--------|\\n| 1 | IDA* heuristic independence | 2 | ✅ Pass |\\n| 2 | No path found (start surrounded) | 4 | ✅ Pass |\\n| 3 | Start equals end | 5 | ✅ Pass |\\n| 4 | Drag during search (state machine) | 1 | ✅ Documented |\\n| 5 | Wall on start/end position | 4 | ✅ Pass |\\n| 6 | Pause/Resume cycle | 1 | ✅ Documented |\\n| 7 | Restart during search | 1 | ✅ Documented |\\n| 8 | JPS all 4 diagonal modes | 4 | ✅ Pass |\\n| 9 | Bi-directional vs unidirectional | 1 | ✅"]
[199.469955, "o", " Pass |\\n| 10 | Weight parameter effect | 1 | ✅ Pass |\\n| 11 | IDA* time limit | 3 | ✅ Pass |\\n| 12 | Full grid walls | 3 | ✅ Pass |\\n| 13 | Large grid performance (64×36) | 2 | ✅ Pass |\\n| 14 | Adjacent start/end | 4 | ✅ Pass |\\n\\n## Key Findings\\n\\n1. **Finders don't validate start/end walkability.** They push start into open list unconditionally. Visual app handles this via `isStartOrEndPos` guard in `mousedown` handler.\\n\\n2. **JPS UI gap confirmed.** Only `IfAtMostOneObstacle` and `Never` exposed. `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` work at library level but need UI dropdown to be selectable. Panel.js hardcodes `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` at line 139.\\n\\n3. **State machine correctly guards drag.** `dragStart`/`dragEnd` only allowed from `ready`/`finished` states. No drag possible during `searching`/`paused`.\\n\\n4. **Pause/resume is clean.** `loop()` checks `Controller.is('searching')` — pausing stops the loop, resume re-enters it from same operations array position.\\n\\n5. **No \\\"pa"]
[199.47026, "o", "th not found\\\" UI feedback.** `view.js:drawPath` returns silently on empty path. `showStats` shows `length: 0` but no explicit message. This is a UI gap, not a library bug.\\n\\n## Full Suite Result\\n\\n```\\n256 passing (1s)\\n0 failing\\n```\\n\\nNo regressions introduced.\\n\",\"numLines\":51,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":51}}}\r\n"]
[211.40131, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_01VUxZfJLueovbTtqoYnzSJo\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01UPUGs1wTkggMsUNbBGcUkK\",\"name\":\"Write\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/scenario-builder/output/summary.md\",\"content\":\"# Scenario Builder — Summary\\n\\n## Test Files\\n\\n- `test/VisualScenarios.BugValidation.js` — 71 new tests covering all 20 assignments\\n- `test/VisualScenarios.js` — 39 pre-existing scenario tests (unchanged)\\n\\n## Results\\n\\n- **New tests: 71 passing, 0 failing**\\n- **Full suite: 465 passing, 0 failing** (no regressions)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Priority 1 — Bug Validation Scenarios (9 tests)\\n\\n| # | Bug | Verified | Detail |\\n|---|-----|----------|--------|\\n| 1 | CSS hover selector typo | YES | `#hide_instruction:hover` at style.css:59 missing 's'. Hover underline never applies to `#hide_instructions` link. |\\n| 2 | Instructions panel one-"]
[211.401621, "o", "way dismiss | YES | `slideUp()` only, no `slideDown`/`slideToggle`. Panel gone for session after click. |\\n| 3 | \\\"Clear Walls\\\" clears everything | YES | Button label says \\\"Clear Walls\\\" but callback is `this.reset` which calls `clearAll()` + `buildNewGrid()`. Clears walls AND path AND footprints AND rebuilds grid. |\\n| 4 | IDA* weight spinner wrong name | YES | `name=\\\"astar_weight\\\"` in `#ida_section` (index.html:103). Works because `panel.js` scopes query to `#ida_section input[name=astar_weight]`. |\\n| 5 | Parent attribute not visualized | YES | `case 'parent':` in view.js:170 is a no-op with XXX comment. `supportedOperations` excludes 'parent'. No parent arrows drawn during search. |\\n\\n## Priority 2 — Core Visual Scenarios (34 tests)\\n\\n| # | Scenario | Tests | Status |\\n|---|----------|-------|--------|\\n| 6 | Open Grid — all algorithms | 22 | All 11 algorithms find path, path length finite & positive |\\n| 7 | Blocked Grid — solid wall | 13 | 6 algorithms return empty path, no crashes, pathLeng"]
[211.401668, "o", "th([])==0 |\\n| 8 | Start==End | 6 | All tested finders handle gracefully, pathLength==0, no NaN |\\n| 9 | Pause/Resume | 2 | Verified loop() checks `is('searching')`, resume calls `loop()` |\\n| 10 | Drag in Finished State | 2 | State machine allows dragStart/dragEnd from 'finished' |\\n\\n## Priority 3 — Algorithm Comparison Scenarios (8 tests)\\n\\n| # | Scenario | Tests | Finding |\\n|---|----------|-------|---------|\\n| 11 | Diagonal Toggle | 1 | Diagonal path shorter than orthogonal (confirmed) |\\n| 12 | Don't Cross Corners | 1 | dontCrossCorners path >= non-restricted path |\\n| 13 | Bi-directional | 1 | Both uni/bi find valid paths through obstacles |\\n| 14 | IDA* Time Limit | 3 | Tiny limit may timeout, generous limit works, -1 skips check |\\n| 15 | JPS vs A* Expansion | 1 | JPS opens fewer nodes than A* on open grid |\\n| 16 | Weighted A* | 1 | weight=1 path <= weight=5 path length |\\n| 17 | Orth JPS vs BFS | 1 | Same path length on same obstacle grid |\\n\\n## Priority 4 — Missing UI Features (8 tests, doc"]
[211.401718, "o", "ument only)\\n\\n| # | Gap | Detail |\\n|---|-----|--------|\\n| 18 | JPS diagonal modes | `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` work at library level. panel.js hardcodes `IfAtMostOneObstacle`. No UI entry point. |\\n| 19 | Animation speed | `operationsPerSecond: 300` hardcoded in controller.js:95. No UI control. |\\n| 20 | Grid size | `gridSize: [64, 36]` hardcoded in controller.js:94. No UI control. |\\n\\n## Bugs Confirmed (not fixed — documenting only per assignment scope)\\n\\n1. **CSS typo**: `#hide_instruction:hover` → should be `#hide_instructions:hover`\\n2. **One-way instructions dismiss**: No way to re-show after `slideUp()`\\n3. **Misleading button label**: \\\"Clear Walls\\\" does full reset\\n4. **Wrong input name**: IDA* weight uses `name=\\\"astar_weight\\\"` (works by accident — scoped selector)\\n5. **Parent visualization missing**: No-op in view.js, no visual indicator for parent relationships\\n\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":"]
